# Python. Docker anchors a pattern to the context root, so `.venv/` alone
# excluded /.venv and let apps/api/.venv (438 MB) into every image build;
# the `**/` forms cover the nested copies too.
**/.venv/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
**/*.pyo
**/.mypy_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/
**/.pytest_cache/
**/*.egg-info/

# Node
**/node_modules/
**/.next/
apps/web/playwright-report/
apps/web/test-results/
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# Local Next.js env overrides — NEVER bake these into an image.
# Audit 2026-07-26 (K3): Dockerfile.frontend does `COPY apps/web/ ./`, so a
# developer's .env.local (which sets NEXT_PUBLIC_AUTH_DISABLED=true) was being
# compiled into the production bundle, disabling authentication entirely:
# every visitor became the `dev@local` admin, /login skipped its redirect and
# "Sign out" became a no-op. Build-time NEXT_PUBLIC_* values must come from the
# compose build args only.
apps/web/.env.local
apps/web/.env.*.local

# The same class of leak on the backend side. Dockerfile.backend does
# `COPY apps/ apps/` and `COPY data/ data/`: without these lines a developer's
# apps/api/.env (JWT and object-store secrets) and the live-malware mirror the
# worker keeps under data/samples/ would be baked into the image layers.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
**/bootstrap.env
# A sample is live malware whatever its name, and a working copy keeps samples
# in more than one samples directory (apps/api/data/samples/ too) and in work
# directories inside them. A list of extensions let every other name through.
# The first line leaves out every file below any data/samples/; the exceptions
# let back in only JSON files directly inside the three fixture directories
# the repository tracks; the last line leaves out again anything below one of
# those, a directory named like a JSON file included. Every line matches the
# file itself, so the rule holds on builders that check a file's parents only
# at the pattern's own depth (Docker Engine 20.10, docker-py) as on those that
# check every parent (BuildKit 0.10 and later, Engine 23 and later). Any *.json
# directly in a fixture directory is kept by design, whatever it holds.
# Uploads and sandbox reports stay out wherever they sit.
# tests/unit/test_no_sample_reaches_an_image_context.py holds this.
**/data/samples/**
!data/samples/dynamic/*.json
!data/samples/network/*.json
!data/samples/static/*.json
**/data/samples/*/*/**
**/data/uploads/
**/data/cape_reports/
data/external/
data/sigma_rules/
models/
logs/
other/
.superpowers/
external/

# Git & IDE
.git/
.github/
.gitattributes

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Docker (prevent recursive context)
docker/

# Build artifacts & logs
*.log
reports/

# Never copied into any image: the documentation (the site under apps/docs with
# its sources, images, dependencies and build output, and docs/examples) and
# the test suite, which the compose stack bind-mounts from the host instead.
apps/docs/
docs/
tests/
